we've got some breaking news um  out of washington dc  the us supreme court there have  overturned  the landmark roe versus wade ruling that  ruling legalized abortion  nationwide and we're trying to go to  our correspondent martha kellner who's  outside the us supreme court in  washington  sir martha roe versus wade has been  overturned  [Applause]  it certainly has this is a seismic  moment for life and law in america you  can see  behind me the protesters gathering here  some of them celebrating and hugging  those are the pro-life crowds those who  are anti-abortion there are also people  here who are devastated those are the  pro-choice pro-abortion  campaigners they've been waiting for  this moment waiting to hear what the  supreme court decided on this hugely  consequential case  they were expecting this decision we had  a draft opinion which was leaked last  month to an american political website  politico which indicated that the  supreme court justices which are the  highest  judges in the land were minded to  overturn the landmark roe versus wave  ruling which legalized abortion  nationwide in america  that this has now been confirmed doesn't  make it any less of an earthquake  just to put it into context this  dismantles  50 years of legal precedent it was 1973  when women across america were given the  right to choose abortion that has now  been reversed from today  many many millions of women across  america will no longer have the right to  access abortion it's been taken away  from the constitution it's the first  time in history a constitutional right  like this has been  removed  as of today we expect that 25 or 26 of  the 50 states  in america will severely restrict  orban abortion vast swathes of the  southern states of america the likes of  texas louisiana arkansas mississippi  also vast waves of the midwest places  like missouri michigan wisconsin places  where millions and millions of women  live they will no longer have the right  to access abortion as they did  yesterday  it really is a massive  massive moment for america it's  something that pro-life anti-abortion  campaigners  have been asking for  for decades and it's been made possible  by a newly right-leaning supreme court  if i can just briefly explain the  make-up of the supreme court it's the  nine highest judges in the land and they  affect uh they affect the biggest legal  decisions in the land and it's now more  conservative leaning than it has been  for decades that's because when former  president donald trump was in charge he  appointed three conservative supreme  court justices to the court  they are determined uh to take this  court more right-leaning and as such  they made the decision yesterday  which expanded gun rights today they've  taken the decision to reverse  abortion rights  it really does mean that america already  so bitterly divided will become  even more divided there will be two  different americas when it comes to  abortion  it's roughly divided like the electoral  maps so you might see  blue states and red states lit up on  that electoral map that you'll remember  from presidential  election nights it roughly follows the  same trend when it comes to abortion so  the red states the republican states  will further restrict or even ban  completely abortion whereas the blue  states  will uh maintain access to abortion so  you'll have this divided america where  women living in blue states will  continue to be able to access abortion  whereas women  living in red states will no longer be  able to access abortions unless they can  afford to travel across state lines so  you'll have a situation where rich women  living in republican states will have  access to abortion women in democrat  states will have access to abortion but  poor women living in republican states  disproportionately women of color will  no longer have access to abortion and  there really is the potential for this  country to become even more vitally  divided  because of this historic decision today
 

